@* Orientation is a parameter the recipe reads, not a class to remember: it decides which edge
   the joins are on, and vertical also flips the group to a column. This demoed nothing at all
   until the component had the parameter — Orientation="vertical" was landing on the div as an
   unknown attribute and the group stayed a row. *@
<div class="flex items-start gap-8">
    <ButtonGroup aria-label="Range">
        <Button Variant="outline">Day</Button>
        <Button Variant="outline">Week</Button>
        <Button Variant="outline">Month</Button>
    </ButtonGroup>

    <ButtonGroup Orientation="vertical" aria-label="Media controls" Class="h-fit">
        <Button Variant="outline" Size="icon"><Icon Name="plus" /></Button>
        <Button Variant="outline" Size="icon"><Icon Name="minus" /></Button>
    </ButtonGroup>
</div>
